  "description": "The v2 inbox sunset (SPEC §3.4) and the v3 re-bind of a v2 device. A v2 bind names no Nostr key, so before 2027-01-21T00:00:00Z it authorizes its event.pubkey only while no v3 record of the device exists and one key carries it; from 2027-01-21T00:00:00Z, by the reader's clock, it authorizes no key. It stays live for sealing to device_pk throughout. The re-bind is the same device as v3 with the same created_at, so a revocation of the device retires it; v3_rebind_later, a re-bind dated after that revocation, is what §3.4 forbids, and stays live. The address and key are BIP-322's own published test vector key (P2WPKH, mainnet); never use them for anything real.",
